   "daf": "24b",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "הַנִּטְעָן עַל אֵשֶׁת אִישׁ וְכוּ׳. אָמַר רַב: וּבְעֵדִים.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that «one who was suspected of» relations with «a married woman» may not marry her even after she divorces her husband. Even if they marry without permission, they must divorce. «Rav said: This is» only in a case when there were «witnesses» to her infidelity, and because of their testimony the court required her first husband divorce her. However, if her first husband divorced her due to suspicion and rumors but without witnesses, her second husband would not be obligated to divorce her."
  }
